# the Israeli report, more words, each with its paradigm in apertium-ita.ita.dix
# and no English word, or with a first word that is another thing: `crímenes
# asesinos' are murderous crimes (`omicida'), `los sospechosos' are suspects
# (`sospettato'), `un incidente armado' an armed one, `se clamó a la venganza'
# was cried out for vengeance (`vendetta', where `revenge' is `rivincita'),
# `una escalada de violencia' an escalation (Italian says `escalation'), `un
# sepelio multitudinario' a crowded funeral, and `aparecieron desnudos'
# appeared naked -- `apparire', where the entry that has it is marked for one
# direction and `figurare' was the word written
<e><p><l>murderous<s n="adj"/></l><r>omicida<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
