<e><p><l>impassion<s n="vblex"/></l><r>appassionare<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
# the Clot street report (AnCora CESS-CAST-P-20000701-80), from Spanish: the
# Italian words for the English ones the Spanish entries above read. Each has
# its paradigm in apertium-ita.ita.dix and no English word, `pedonale' and
# `pedonalizzazione' for the pedestrian street, `paletto' for a bollard,
# `preventivare' for a work budgeted at so many millions, `sconto' and
# `disaccordo' for a discount and a disagreement, `interessato' for the traders
# affected and `previsto' for a planned length (`godere' is in the store
# already, `usufruire' coming first in the dictionary)
<e><p><l>pedestrian<s n="adj"/></l><r>pedonale<s n="adj"/><s n="mf"/></r></p></e>
